   "faq2_q": "How long does a typical automation project take?",
   "faq2_a": "It depends entirely on what we're building. If it's an AI agent for a specific niche problem, the timeline follows the complexity of the task — I won't spend more time than the job needs. That could be one or two days, or one or two months.\n\nIf you want an actual assessment, call me or write with your specifics. We don't do corporate bull-shit, so I try to be as transparent as possible.",
   "faq3_q": "What if I don't want to pay upfront?",
   "faq3_a": "That's fine — depending on the project, we don't need upfront payment at all.\n\nIf I'm building software for the company, expect to pay a deposit and then a payment against each agreed milestone. That's very normal.\n\nWhat I also offer is a performance-based option: taking a percentage of the company's income over a defined period, instead of a fixed fee. This is easy to arrange, and it's what I usually do for projects where I can help you get significantly more out of the process — rather than delivering the product and then leaving.",
   "faq4_q": "Do you provide ongoing support after project completion?",
   "faq4_a": "Absolutely — if you have the need for it.\n\nMy goal is always to hand the work over in a way that fits you, so you're not dependent on me. That said, there's usually a period of one to three months, depending on the project, where I help out with further iterations, new features, or maintaining the project until you've found someone else to take it on. Most of the systems I build maintain themselves with very little input, so it shouldn't be a problem at all.\n\nIf you want a \"tech person on speed dial\", that won't be free forever — but I'm glad to help smaller businesses with tasks that aren't too time-consuming.",
   "faq5_q": "What's included in a free consultation?",
   "faq5_a": "You tell me some of the frustrations you're running into. I ask questions to understand your processes and your business. Then I give you clear, actionable advice and solutions — free, and they don't necessarily involve my services.\n\nYou'd be surprised how far you can get with free tools, without paying a third party to come into your business and make changes or additions.\n\nNo sales pitch, and absolutely no commitment.",
